The '''Resonant Chamber''' is a small, RF-quiet, magnetically-clean room used for bench-grade [[Psi-Tech]] calibration smf single-operator deep-state sessions. Engineered with a faraday-screened + mu-metal-lined + acoustically-treated room with a calibrated Coherence Beacon and instrumented seat.

== Overview ==

A Chamber session involves:

* '''Operator seated''' in an instrumented chair; HelmKit + [[Psi Recorder]] + [[Field Recorder]] all active.
* '''Background characterized''' — known [[Coherence Beacon]] reference; measured residual mains hum; documented ambient RF; airflow noise floor.
* '''Protocol run''' — baseline, stressor, recovery; or single-operator deep-state under operator-controlled [[Psi Stabilizer]] anchor; or pair-bond [[Psi Tether]] characterization.
* '''Records exported''' — signed sessions to [[Resonant Pipeline]] with chamber metadata stamp.

The Chamber is the place where measurements get their floor: anything seen here that vanishes outside is a chamber artifact; anything seen outside that is also seen here is real.

